  "configuration_id": "config_046",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, singleprofile, weighted) achieves 0.523 acc while config_004 (image_only, resnet50, singleprofile) achieves only 0.208 acc, a ~31 pp gap. However, we have no RNA-only data point, so we cannot decompose how much of the multimodal performance comes from the RNA modality versus the image modality or their interaction. Question: config_046 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000, no image, no aggregation, no fusion) isolates the RNA contribution using the same RNA encoder and profile setting as config_018, with no other confounds. Why best next experiment: With only two completed runs, the single most important uncertainty is the per-modality contribution. Knowing RNA-only accuracy lets us determine whether the multimodal gain is driven primarily by RNA (suggesting we should invest in better RNA encoders like scgpt/scvi) or by the image+RNA interaction (suggesting we should focus on fusion and image encoder upgrades). This single clean comparison maximally reduces uncertainty before committing further budget to more complex multiprofile or aggregation variants."
}

